    "created_at": "2022-10-21T08:27:57Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-10-21T08:27:57Z",
    "body": "> I guess \"[DOMHighResTimeStamp](https://w3c.github.io/hr-time/#dom-domhighrestimestamp) representing the high resolution time at which the [shared monotonic clock](https://w3c.github.io/hr-time/#dfn-shared-monotonic-clock) is zero\" is supposed to be the Unix epoch?\r\n\r\nNo, zero-monotonic is implementation/OS specific, and has an offset from unix epoch which (in chrome) is constant for the duration of the browser runtime.",
