    "updated_at": "2022-10-21T14:25:40Z",
    "body": "I'm writing the change because https://github.com/WICG/turtledove/pull/378 and https://wicg.github.io/attribution-reporting-api/ use the concepts without having a central place to define them. The integration with performance timing is a place where time gets more complicated the longer you look at it. You wind up having to define extra clocks (like the monotonic one), and we might want to say that each instant is associated with a particular clock. Then you get into TAI vs UTC, and relativistic situations, and ..., and I think it's worth starting with the simplification that specs actually use before trying to explain all the details.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
